Indigo Hammer Doctrine: Before adding complexity, search for a collapsed distinction. Split the overloaded concept into its minimal semantic operators (ZPC), then reconnect only those operators that continue to add predictive or explanatory value (Kintsugi). The repaired structure should preserve both the original capability and explicit knowledge of its former failure mode, making each crack a permanent source of increased robustness rather than something hidden.